              },
              "declarationKind": "export",
              "jsDoc": {
                "doc": "Starts the native streams proxy and its factory-owned upstream server.\n\nAuth is asserted before any environment, storage or listener access. Auth and serve objects,\nand caller CORS arrays, retain identity. Only omitted protocol arrays receive copied defaults.\nThe native running handle drains the front listener and stops the upstream through its shutdown\nhook. Before that handle exists, startup failure attempts native upstream stop and preserves the\nidentical primary error even if cleanup rejects. No unrelated or global resources are closed.\n",
                "tags": [
                  {
                    "kind": "param",
                    "name": "options",
                    "doc": "Required native auth posture and optional CORS/listener configuration."
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "return",
                    "doc": "The native running handle; its stop and caller signal use native drain semantics."
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "throws",
                    "tsType": {
                      "repr": "TypeError",
                      "kind": "typeRef",
                      "value": {
                        "typeName": "TypeError",
                        "resolution": {
                          "kind": "typeParam"
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "doc": "When the caller's auth posture is invalid."
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "throws",
                    "tsType": {
                      "repr": "Error",
                      "kind": "typeRef",
                      "value": {
                        "typeName": "Error",
                        "resolution": {
                          "kind": "typeParam"
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "doc": "When no explicit port or host PORT/STREAMS_PORT value is available.\n"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "example",
                    "doc": "Guarded streams service on an ephemeral loopback port\n```ts\nimport { createStaticCredentialAuthenticator } from '@netscript/service/auth';\nimport { startStreamsService } from '@netscript/plugin-streams/service';\n\nconst authenticator = createStaticCredentialAuthenticator({\n  credentials: { local: { subject: 'service:streams', scopes: [], roles: ['service'] } },\n});\nconst running = await startStreamsService({\n  auth: { authn: { authenticator } },\n  serve: { hostname: '127.0.0.1', port: 0 },\n});\nconsole.log(running.addr.port);\nawait running.stop();\n```"
                  }
                ]
              },
